'''''Urtica morifolia''''' is a species of [[plant]] in the nettle family [[Urticaceae]]. 

==Description==
It is a perennial [[subshrub]] that grows in the subtropical biome.<ref name=":1">{{Cite web |title=Urtica morifolia Poir. {{!}} Plants of the World Online {{!}} Kew Science |url=http://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:857758-1 |access-date=2025-08-07 |website=Plants of the World Online |language=en}}</ref><ref name=":0">{{Cite web |title=Urtica morifolia |url=http://www.floradecanarias.com/urtica_morifolia.html |access-date=2025-08-07 |website=www.floradecanarias.com}}</ref>

==Distribution==
It is native to the [[Canary Islands]] and [[Madeira (Assembly of the Republic constituency)|Madeira]]. It was introduced into the [[Azores]].<ref name=":1" />

